1
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:47,520
Hey, Mungkorn! Don't fall asleep!
Someone help me!

2
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:49,040
Looks like the pain
is starting to hit him.

3
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:51,400
-They have to be around here somewhere.
-Find a place to hide.

4
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:53,520
Get down. Now!

5
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,920
You'll be the one hunting them down.

6
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,240
I surrender.

7
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:00,000
Please spare us. I surrender.

8
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:01,840
Bring me to your boss.

9
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,800
<i>Someone tipped off the Thai authorities</i>

10
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:04,920
<i>about our call center operation.</i>

11
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,640
If you take them all down,

12
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:07,880
I'll pay you a million baht per head.

13
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:09,200
Gladly.

14
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:12,520
My last memory of my dad

15
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:16,080
<i>is when I saw him pickpocketing a man</i>
<i>at a train station.</i>

16
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:17,560
<i>I was so shocked.</i>

17
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:21,839
<i>Seeing him do that made me realize</i>

18
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:24,600
my dad might not be the good man
I believed he was.

19
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:27,320
-Pao!
-Ris! Koh!

20
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:30,480
Hey, Chen! Easy!

21
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:33,440
I can't breathe. That's enough.

22
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:34,800
Ms. Lin's here too?

23
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:39,080
I'm here to bring everyone back
under Admin's orders.

24
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:41,320
I've already prepared
escape routes for everyone.

25
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:42,560
Right now,

26
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:45,240
Admin wants you all to regroup

27
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:46,560
for the final mission.

28
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:50,560
The final mission?

29
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:54,080
We're going to finish Louis off.

30
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:05,280
We're finally getting out of here. Get in.

31
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,480
Let's go.

32
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,680
Let's go, Yak. Drive fast.

33
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:09,720
Alright.

34
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,360
Good luck, Oab.

35
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:13,520
Thank you so much for everything, Risa.

36
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:17,920
Thank you too, Dr. Koh.

37
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:22,480
Good luck, you little troublemaker.

38
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:25,680
Please stay safe, everyone.

39
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:31,160
-Are we going to make it?
-We've got this.

40
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:33,000
I hope the money I gave you

41
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:35,360
can keep Oab from doing dangerous jobs.

42
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:37,760
Yes, I promise.

43
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:41,520
Good luck, Oab.

44
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:43,960
Take care of yourself.

45
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,520
-Let's go.
-Yeah.

46
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:16,640
Everyone, there's a checkpoint up ahead.

47
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:17,800
Huh?

48
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:24,280
Didn't Lin say everything was cleared?
How is there still a checkpoint?

49
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,680
Yeah.

50
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:28,760
What's up, guys? What do we do?
Just ram through it?

51
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:46,840
Are you Thai?

52
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:49,200
Show your passports and IDs.

53
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,280
-Driver.
-Yes.

54
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:54,480
Step out here.

55
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:57,320
Okay, okay. Hold on.

56
00:05:57,400 --> 00:05:59,080
Take it easy, alright?

57
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:02,760
I thought everything had been cleared.

58
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:05,680
Are you sure it was cleared?

59
00:06:13,680 --> 00:06:15,120
Everyone, get down!

60
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:10,520
MR. WISUT

61
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,160
MR. WISUT

62
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,520
MR. WISUT

63
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:19,040
I've taken care of them,
just like you asked.

64
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:22,520
Don't forget your promise.

65
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:39,000
Behind you!

66
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:54,720
<i>Now moving on to politics.</i>

67
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:57,920
<i>This is breaking news</i>
<i>regarding a parliamentary candidate</i>

68
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,520
<i>from the Charoen Thai Party.</i>

69
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:02,880
<i>We've received insider information</i>

70
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:05,520
<i>that the Charoen Thai Party is preparing</i>
<i>to nominate Boss Louis,</i>

71
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:09,680
<i>also known as Kacha Paisalkriangkrai,</i>
<i>owner of H Pharmacy,</i>

72
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:11,960
<i>as a party-list MP candidate.</i>

73
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,600
<i>In this case,</i>

74
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:17,760
<i>Boss Louis is being seen</i>
<i>as a young, rising businessman</i>

75
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:19,800
<i>entering politics.</i>

76
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:31,400
Hello.

77
00:08:33,560 --> 00:08:34,720
This way, please.

78
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:40,680
About the vote on the bill,

79
00:08:40,760 --> 00:08:43,359
I'll need your side's support.

80
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:46,839
Please wait here for a moment.
He's on a call.

81
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:50,640
As for the position
in the ministry you requested,

82
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:52,680
there won't be any problem at all.

83
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,400
Thank you very much, sir.

84
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:03,320
Thank you for supporting me,

85
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:05,160
just as you promised.

86
00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:08,200
What are you talking about?

87
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:13,400
I've done everything you ordered.

88
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:15,560
Those people are all dead in Poipet.

89
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:18,760
Who told you to leak this to the press?

90
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:20,400
Well…

91
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:23,400
It wasn't me who leaked it.

92
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:25,080
If it wasn't you,
then who the hell was it?

93
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:29,960
Don't think I don't see
your greed and ambition.

94
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:33,680
But you promised me.

95
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:36,480
Do you really think
becoming an MP is that easy?

96
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:40,160
Are you even ready for it?

97
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:43,480
Your illegal businesses
aren't even cleaned up yet.

98
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:45,520
Go back and do your job properly.

99
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:48,520
When the time is right,

100
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:50,200
I'll let you know.

101
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,760
And don't make any more mistakes.

102
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:57,400
Yes, sir.

103
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:18,760
Alright, you can come out now.

104
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:26,880
Before cancer kills me,
this stupid bag is going to.

105
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:31,000
I almost died for real.

106
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:34,640
Captain, you're safe, right?

107
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:38,840
This is for betraying me.

108
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:45,080
Let's think of it

109
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:48,240
as a bonus, Captain.

110
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:51,840
That beautiful lady paid me very well.

111
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:55,440
Help! Somebody help me!

112
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:56,840
Help!

113
00:10:56,920 --> 00:10:58,080
24 HOURS EARLIER

114
00:10:58,160 --> 00:10:59,200
Help!

115
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:03,200
Who's there?

116
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:05,960
Are you one of them?

117
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:13,040
I'll cut you loose and let you go

118
00:11:14,280 --> 00:11:15,920
if you accept my offer.

119
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:17,520
What offer?

120
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:20,520
An offer to change your mind.

121
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:25,960
Help us.

122
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:29,600
How can I trust

123
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:31,680
you're not one of them?

124
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:35,400
I'll bring you their bodies to prove it.

125
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:37,400
Mr. Louis, we've got a problem.

126
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:38,560
What is it?

127
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:48,280
Hello.

128
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:52,280
We're making a small change to the plan.
We're going to die here.

129
00:11:53,440 --> 00:11:55,520
-What?
-There are fake blood packs

130
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:57,040
under everyone's seats.

131
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:03,440
The blood is fake,
but the bullets are real.

132
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:08,120
Tell everyone to stay low and take cover.

133
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:10,080
See you in Bangkok.

134
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:17,320
Everyone, there's a checkpoint up ahead.

135
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:21,160
What's up, guys? What do we do?
Just ram through it?

136
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:25,440
No, bro. Everyone,
this is all part of Admin's plan.

137
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:29,480
Driver, step out here.

138
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:32,400
Okay, okay. Hold on.

139
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:34,080
Take it easy, alright?

140
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:36,400
Why are you making this so dramatic?

141
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:38,400
I thought everything had been cleared.

142
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:40,440
Are you sure it was cleared?

143
00:12:42,640 --> 00:12:43,760
Everyone, get down!

144
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:03,160
Gao, hey!

145
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:06,440
Do you have any fake blood left?
I don't have any on me.

146
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:09,880
Why are you yelling? You're going
to ruin the plan. I'm out of fake blood.

147
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:12,040
What am I supposed to do?

148
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:14,240
That fake soldier
made me get out of my seat.

149
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:16,360
I didn't grab mine.
You expect me to go back for it?

150
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:17,280
Are you crazy?

151
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:19,520
Use mine. I've still got a little left.

152
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:23,840
What are you doing?

153
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:26,640
Hurry up. I need to shoot a video for him.

154
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,320
That's enough.

155
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:34,920
Whoever pays me more,

156
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:37,840
that's who I work for.

157
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:40,080
Don't be mad, Captain.

158
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:42,720
So what's next?

159
00:13:42,800 --> 00:13:44,400
I've already arranged a vehicle for you.

160
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:47,320
You need to get back to Bangkok tonight.

161
00:13:47,920 --> 00:13:49,520
What vehicle? Where is it?

162
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:53,880
Want to see it? Come with me.

163
00:13:57,680 --> 00:13:58,520
You're so extra.

164
00:13:58,600 --> 00:13:59,640
Wait.

165
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:04,200
I'm coming too.

166
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:14,640
Before we leave, I need to wash up.

167
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:17,400
This fake blood is making me feel sticky.

168
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:21,000
Yeah, I feel sticky too, Hong.

169
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:23,800
Good idea. Let's go

170
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:25,440
take a shower and clean up together.

171
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:29,280
Hey. Don't try to be slick, you pervert.

172
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:30,960
What do you mean, pervert, Gao?

173
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:33,880
I'm just taking a shower with her.
What's wrong with that?

174
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:35,760
Listen.

175
00:14:35,840 --> 00:14:37,560
The second we make up,

176
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:39,200
your true colors come out, you jerk.

177
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:42,000
Enough. Stop fighting over it.

178
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:44,200
The three of us can just go together.

179
00:14:45,680 --> 00:14:47,520
-Take a shower?
-All three of us?

180
00:14:48,640 --> 00:14:50,000
Who said anything about taking a shower?

181
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:51,800
-Then what?
-Cleaning ourselves up.

182
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:57,120
Hong.

183
00:14:57,200 --> 00:15:00,280
-I'll clean you up.
-I'll help too.

184
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:03,240
Going through all that danger in Poipet
wasn't for nothing.

185
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,160
What do you mean, Chen?

186
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:07,080
When we help each other like this,

187
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:09,000
we end up growing closer.

188
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:14,680
Anyway, want to go get cleaned up?

189
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:20,120
<i>We've obtained new leads</i>
<i>in the call center investigation,</i>

190
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:22,440
<i>including the cases involving</i>
<i>Mam Yollada and Boss Kluay.</i>

191
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:25,720
<i>All three cases are connected,</i>
<i>as they are part</i>

192
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,880
<i>of the same criminal network.</i>

193
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:29,520
<i>My team and I</i>

194
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:33,120
<i>are working to trace</i>
<i>the mastermind behind all of this.</i>

195
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:35,480
If you're watching this,

196
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:37,520
I'm coming for you.

197
00:15:40,680 --> 00:15:42,200
That's our boss.

198
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,360
He's the real deal.

199
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:47,080
Captain, the boss wants to see you.

200
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:48,960
Yes.

201
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:50,480
POL.LT.GEN. THAMMARONG INTHARASA

202
00:15:56,640 --> 00:15:57,600
Permission to enter, sir.

203
00:15:57,680 --> 00:15:58,880
Come in.

204
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:07,520
-You saw the news, right?
-Yes, sir.

205
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:09,360
My source says

206
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:13,600
that gang was ambushed in Poipet.

207
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:16,080
-Is that even possible?
-Exactly.

208
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:18,440
Something that big
and the Cambodian police had no idea.

209
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:22,560
Here.

210
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:26,040
I want you to find out
what they're planning next.

211
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:28,800
But sir,

212
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:31,080
isn't that actually good for us?

213
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:33,120
They're helping us
take down criminals anyway.

214
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:37,000
Catching criminals is our job.

215
00:16:37,680 --> 00:16:39,120
Not theirs.

216
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:42,840
Sorry, sir.

217
00:16:57,160 --> 00:17:01,400
KONGKIAT KAMNERDRAT

218
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:09,480
Welcome home, everyone.

219
00:17:09,560 --> 00:17:11,200
You're welcome, lady.

220
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:15,080
So what's Admin's next move?

221
00:17:15,159 --> 00:17:17,080
Louis thinks you're all dead.

222
00:17:17,159 --> 00:17:18,720
That means,

223
00:17:19,360 --> 00:17:23,159
if you want to stop here
and go back to your normal lives,

224
00:17:23,240 --> 00:17:24,879
this is the best chance you'll get.

225
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:28,280
If Louis finds out we're still alive,

226
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:29,760
he won't let us go that easily.

227
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:35,040
I'll give you some time to think about it.

228
00:17:35,119 --> 00:17:37,280
If a new mission comes up

229
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:38,600
and Admin contacts you again,

230
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:43,360
you can decide whether to accept it

231
00:17:44,040 --> 00:17:44,920
or not.

232
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:53,680
Good luck, everyone. Bye.

233
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:57,280
-Hey.
-Hold on.

234
00:17:57,800 --> 00:18:00,360
What is this? She just comes in,
says a few words, and leaves.

235
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:03,640
Come on. Just tell us what to do,
so we can get it over with, right, Yak?

236
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:05,920
Yeah, this Admin guy

237
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:07,960
-is so extra, right?
-Yeah.

238
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:09,880
He's getting more and more mysterious.

239
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:12,840
But I'm really curious
who Admin actually is.

240
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,160
It's better not to know.

241
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:17,360
If things go wrong, the police
won't be able to trace it back to us.

242
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:20,720
So…

243
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:24,120
Now that we're free. What should we do?

244
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:27,960
-What should we do?
-How about this?

245
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:30,920
Let's go to my place.
I'll cook something nice for everyone.

246
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,160
Hey, I'm in.

247
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:33,920
-I'm in.
-Yeah.

248
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:35,200
No.

249
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:38,320
Don't forget James was a cop,
and he's been to your place before.

250
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:41,000
Even if he's dead,
his people are still around.

251
00:18:41,080 --> 00:18:41,960
Don't take the risk.

252
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:47,880
Wherever you guys go,
just be careful. I'm out.

253
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:48,800
What? Hey.

254
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:51,280
Koh, why are you killing the vibe
all of a sudden?

255
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:53,520
You ruined the mood.
Then I'll take you to a secret spot.

256
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:54,440
What secret spot?

257
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:57,160
A secret spot
where no credit cards are accepted.

258
00:18:57,240 --> 00:18:58,760
A secret spot

259
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:00,800
where nobody can find it.

260
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:02,160
Where is it?

261
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:03,400
The roadside larb shop.

262
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:04,840
I'm serious.

263
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:07,000
It's street food.
Nobody can find us there.

264
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:09,120
-Let's go. Ris, you coming?
-Let's go.

265
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:12,560
You guys go ahead.
I need to talk to Koh for a bit.

266
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:14,120
Huh?

267
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:18,160
Hey, kiddo.

268
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:24,800
Then I'm heading back too.

269
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:27,400
You're leaving already?

270
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,800
Mung.

271
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:55,920
-Try that one. Be careful.
-Come on.

272
00:20:58,760 --> 00:21:00,040
It's going to fall.

273
00:21:00,120 --> 00:21:03,800
Come on.

274
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:11,920
Mungkorn, is that you?

275
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:15,320
Hello, Dad.

276
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:18,360
Where have you been all these days?

277
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:20,200
I was…

278
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:21,720
Oh, Mungkorn.

279
00:21:21,800 --> 00:21:23,280
So you do know how to come home.

280
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:31,160
Come on. Sit down
and talk with your siblings.

281
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:32,240
Come on.

282
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:36,280
It's okay. I'm tired.

283
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:41,720
Mungkorn.

284
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:47,480
Mungkorn.

285
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:50,840
Hey.

286
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:56,240
What happened to your arm?

287
00:21:59,560 --> 00:22:00,840
Just a minor accident.

288
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:02,160
What is it, Dad?

289
00:22:02,800 --> 00:22:03,760
Where have you been?

290
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:07,560
I've had people looking for you
at your condo and the university.

291
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:10,200
Why didn't you go
to your mother's birthday?

292
00:22:10,720 --> 00:22:12,160
Everyone else went.

293
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:16,400
-I didn't want to.
-Why not?

294
00:22:17,520 --> 00:22:18,720
She's not my mother.

295
00:22:23,640 --> 00:22:26,320
Remember this. In this house,

296
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:28,640
we're all one family.

297
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:32,920
I think you should ask the others

298
00:22:33,800 --> 00:22:36,440
whether they see me as family or not.

299
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:43,560
Where do you think you're going?

300
00:22:46,560 --> 00:22:47,640
Mungkorn!

301
00:23:02,800 --> 00:23:04,800
Do you know anyone else

302
00:23:05,320 --> 00:23:07,040
who might know where my dad is?

303
00:23:09,440 --> 00:23:10,960
There is actually one person.

304
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:13,720
He used to work Louis's case
five years ago.

305
00:23:15,120 --> 00:23:19,000
But after Aek disappeared,
he resigned from the police force

306
00:23:19,080 --> 00:23:21,000
and moved abroad.

307
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:24,480
Then how can we contact him?

308
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:26,240
No one can reach him.

309
00:23:27,520 --> 00:23:29,320
Our only hope is Louis.

310
00:23:31,280 --> 00:23:33,480
We have to find him somehow.

311
00:23:41,440 --> 00:23:43,080
What are you going to do about Admin?

312
00:23:45,640 --> 00:23:48,000
I don't know. What about you?

313
00:23:56,720 --> 00:23:57,960
I don't know either.

314
00:24:05,120 --> 00:24:06,400
Hey.

315
00:24:07,640 --> 00:24:10,720
Can I ask you something?

316
00:24:14,800 --> 00:24:16,720
Why did you choose to live like this?

317
00:24:20,040 --> 00:24:23,240
Live like this? Like what?

318
00:24:23,320 --> 00:24:24,440
Well.

319
00:24:25,760 --> 00:24:28,760
The kind of life
where you do illegal things.

320
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:32,360
Have you ever thought about quitting?

321
00:24:34,800 --> 00:24:37,120
No. I just wanted money.

322
00:24:39,080 --> 00:24:40,440
That's it?

323
00:24:45,520 --> 00:24:47,760
I wanted my mother to live comfortably,

324
00:24:48,360 --> 00:24:50,320
so she wouldn't have to suffer
like before.

325
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:54,120
Does it have anything to do

326
00:24:54,680 --> 00:24:58,080
with that guy calling you
the son of a servant?

327
00:25:03,040 --> 00:25:05,000
My mother used to be a maid
at James's house.

328
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:11,000
Back then, everything we did
was always wrong,

329
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:15,960
<i>so much so that we started believing</i>
<i>it was because we were poor.</i>

330
00:25:18,120 --> 00:25:18,960
Koh.

331
00:25:19,040 --> 00:25:19,720
22 YEARS AGO

332
00:25:19,800 --> 00:25:22,000
Can you go mop
outside Madam's room for me?

333
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:23,880
Yes, Mom.

334
00:25:54,840 --> 00:25:56,160
What are you looking at?

335
00:25:58,720 --> 00:26:01,320
I really didn't take that money, ma'am.

336
00:26:01,400 --> 00:26:04,360
If you didn't take it,
then how did my 5,000 baht disappear?

337
00:26:06,600 --> 00:26:08,080
Was it your son? Huh?

338
00:26:08,160 --> 00:26:09,680
No, ma'am.

339
00:26:10,200 --> 00:26:12,240
I never taught my child to steal.

340
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:14,840
Mom.

341
00:26:16,280 --> 00:26:17,480
I saw Koh take it.

342
00:26:18,480 --> 00:26:21,400
That's not true. I didn't take it.

343
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:23,720
Are you calling me a liar? This morning,

344
00:26:23,800 --> 00:26:26,800
I saw you hanging around
outside my mom's room.

345
00:26:30,440 --> 00:26:32,400
Koh, did you take it?

346
00:26:33,840 --> 00:26:35,160
Why would you do that?

347
00:26:35,240 --> 00:26:36,760
Didn't I teach you

348
00:26:36,840 --> 00:26:38,320
not to take other people's things?

349
00:26:38,920 --> 00:26:41,200
I've taught you already.
Why can't you remember?

350
00:26:41,800 --> 00:26:43,920
Don't be a thief.

351
00:26:44,440 --> 00:26:46,360
I told you before. Why can't you remember?

352
00:26:47,920 --> 00:26:49,680
Why did you steal other people's things?

353
00:26:49,760 --> 00:26:52,520
Why do you want things that aren't yours?

354
00:27:10,480 --> 00:27:11,680
What are you looking at?

355
00:27:14,640 --> 00:27:15,800
James.

356
00:27:17,040 --> 00:27:19,360
I saw you steal your mom's money.

357
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:21,560
Why did you say it was me?

358
00:27:23,400 --> 00:27:25,080
So what if I lied?

359
00:27:27,680 --> 00:27:28,880
Who cares about the truth?

360
00:27:30,640 --> 00:27:32,760
Poor people are always thieves.

361
00:27:33,560 --> 00:27:35,240
Right, son of a servant?

362
00:27:36,240 --> 00:27:37,560
<i>Since that day,</i>

363
00:27:38,920 --> 00:27:40,840
<i>I always believed</i>

364
00:27:42,640 --> 00:27:44,000
that if you had money,

365
00:27:45,640 --> 00:27:47,120
you could buy justice.

366
00:27:52,160 --> 00:27:53,440
And now,

367
00:27:54,400 --> 00:27:55,960
do you still think that way?

368
00:27:56,760 --> 00:28:00,240
Even after growing up
and understanding more,

369
00:28:00,840 --> 00:28:02,680
isn't the world still the same?

370
00:28:04,840 --> 00:28:06,400
Money can still buy everything.

371
00:28:09,160 --> 00:28:11,880
But I think the reason
your life is so chaotic now

372
00:28:12,720 --> 00:28:13,920
is because of money, isn't it?

373
00:28:16,320 --> 00:28:18,600
Do you think your mom would be okay

374
00:28:19,160 --> 00:28:21,040
if she knew what you're doing now?

375
00:28:39,360 --> 00:28:41,240
-Let's go, Chen.
-Let's go.

376
00:28:43,760 --> 00:28:46,520
Hey, Angpao. Why are there

377
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:49,440
so many pharmacies opening these days?

378
00:28:49,520 --> 00:28:52,080
Maybe they're just cheap.

379
00:28:52,160 --> 00:28:56,240
Selling cheap shouldn't make them
rich enough to expand this much.

380
00:28:56,320 --> 00:28:59,040
Maybe it's a franchise, Chen.

381
00:28:59,120 --> 00:29:01,040
Here, eat this.

382
00:29:01,640 --> 00:29:05,200
-You're overthinking it.
-Not again. This is going to rot my teeth.

383
00:29:26,680 --> 00:29:27,760
Close the shop.

384
00:29:27,840 --> 00:29:29,280
-No one's coming in.
-Yes, sir.

385
00:29:54,240 --> 00:29:55,600
Is Louis here?

386
00:29:55,680 --> 00:29:57,000
He's at the pool table.

387
00:30:07,200 --> 00:30:08,240
What's up,

388
00:30:08,760 --> 00:30:10,880
Mr. Future MP?

389
00:30:13,840 --> 00:30:15,920
Survived and still running your mouth?

390
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:18,960
Come on. In the end,

391
00:30:19,040 --> 00:30:21,520
we still managed to take down
the Admin gang, right?

392
00:30:22,240 --> 00:30:25,040
Looks like you're getting closer
to becoming an MP.

393
00:30:25,760 --> 00:30:28,360
I even saw the news talking about you.

394
00:30:31,240 --> 00:30:32,720
It's because of those reporters.

395
00:30:32,800 --> 00:30:35,080
Now Wisut's angry with me.

396
00:30:35,920 --> 00:30:37,320
What do you mean? I don't get it.

397
00:30:38,120 --> 00:30:39,520
He claims I leaked information.

398
00:30:40,120 --> 00:30:42,920
That's why he won't push
my MP bid through.

399
00:30:43,440 --> 00:30:45,000
Why would he do that?

400
00:30:46,240 --> 00:30:48,800
He wants to keep me under control
and use me like this.

401
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:51,560
In Wisut's eyes,

402
00:30:51,640 --> 00:30:54,760
I'm the best money launderer he's got.

403
00:30:56,160 --> 00:30:59,320
He just ordered me
to move another large batch of cash.

404
00:31:01,400 --> 00:31:02,320
Are you going to do it?

405
00:31:03,880 --> 00:31:05,440
I don't have a choice.

406
00:31:12,440 --> 00:31:14,960
But when the right moment comes,

407
00:31:16,040 --> 00:31:18,080
I'm going all in.

408
00:31:24,880 --> 00:31:26,640
TWO MEN AND ONE WOMAN NOODLE SHOP

409
00:31:35,640 --> 00:31:36,920
All finished.

410
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:38,880
-Bro, the bill--
-Wait.

411
00:31:39,960 --> 00:31:41,120
What?

412
00:31:41,200 --> 00:31:42,400
Let's get some exercise.

413
00:31:42,480 --> 00:31:43,840
-Huh?
-What do you mean, Hong?

414
00:31:43,920 --> 00:31:44,880
-Run.
-Huh?

415
00:31:45,720 --> 00:31:46,880
-Run!
-Huh?

416
00:31:46,960 --> 00:31:48,920
-Run!
-Hey!

417
00:31:49,000 --> 00:31:51,000
You dined and dashed?

418
00:32:01,600 --> 00:32:02,960
Did he follow us?

419
00:32:03,040 --> 00:32:04,200
Hold on!

420
00:32:04,280 --> 00:32:05,360
-Yak, wait.
-Huh?

421
00:32:05,440 --> 00:32:06,960
Why did you steal their seasonings?

422
00:32:07,040 --> 00:32:08,080
Oh no.

423
00:32:08,600 --> 00:32:10,520
I don't know. I panicked.

424
00:32:11,720 --> 00:32:12,840
Hong.

425
00:32:12,920 --> 00:32:15,160
Why did you dine and dash?
It wasn't that much money.

426
00:32:15,240 --> 00:32:17,480
Hey, it was fun.

427
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:19,520
Feels like the old days, huh?

428
00:32:19,600 --> 00:32:22,000
Stop laughing. We're not young anymore.

429
00:32:22,080 --> 00:32:25,160
I almost passed out from running.
Hong, you're not even feeling well.

430
00:32:25,240 --> 00:32:28,560
It's just a little run.
Builds your strength, okay?

431
00:32:28,640 --> 00:32:29,840
-Gao.
-What?

432
00:32:29,920 --> 00:32:31,320
Should we go return it?

433
00:32:31,400 --> 00:32:33,600
Don't go back.
They'll beat us up for sure.

434
00:32:33,680 --> 00:32:36,520
We already took it.
Fish sauce is expensive. Keep it.

435
00:32:37,840 --> 00:32:38,720
Fine.

436
00:32:57,000 --> 00:32:58,040
What the hell?

437
00:33:12,600 --> 00:33:13,440
Come talk to me for a second.

438
00:33:32,160 --> 00:33:33,160
Get in.

439
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:43,560
I just want a quick word. Won't take long.

440
00:33:47,480 --> 00:33:51,360
Don't worry. There are no cameras
or recording devices in this car.

441
00:33:54,320 --> 00:33:55,640
I haven't introduced myself yet.

442
00:33:55,720 --> 00:33:56,800
I already know

443
00:33:58,120 --> 00:33:59,240
who you are.

444
00:34:01,480 --> 00:34:02,640
Good.

445
00:34:03,760 --> 00:34:06,560
Then we can skip the small talk.

446
00:34:08,440 --> 00:34:10,960
Where is your gang hiding now?

447
00:34:11,880 --> 00:34:12,920
Gang?

448
00:34:13,800 --> 00:34:14,800
What gang?

449
00:34:14,880 --> 00:34:16,560
You might be able to fool Louis.

450
00:34:17,240 --> 00:34:19,160
But you can't fool me.

451
00:34:20,360 --> 00:34:23,200
I don't know what you're talking about.

452
00:34:24,800 --> 00:34:27,959
What is your leader, Admin,
planning this time?

453
00:34:28,039 --> 00:34:31,999
He even staged
everyone's death so perfectly.

454
00:34:39,240 --> 00:34:43,959
Are you seriously going to accuse me
without any evidence, Officer?

455
00:34:44,039 --> 00:34:46,400
That's not very professional.

456
00:34:48,439 --> 00:34:51,320
-I'll be going now.
-If I tell your father about this,

457
00:34:52,680 --> 00:34:54,400
he won't be happy, right?

458
00:35:04,560 --> 00:35:05,479
Yeah.

459
00:35:05,560 --> 00:35:07,479
My dad won't be happy

460
00:35:09,680 --> 00:35:10,600
about you hurting me.

461
00:35:19,680 --> 00:35:22,800
-What are you doing?
-Don't. Let go of him.

462
00:35:27,480 --> 00:35:28,760
Yes.

463
00:35:29,280 --> 00:35:30,800
There's a dashcam in my car.

464
00:35:31,680 --> 00:35:33,840
If you don't let me go properly,

465
00:35:34,360 --> 00:35:38,000
I'll have evidence that you assaulted me.

466
00:35:49,640 --> 00:35:52,520
I don't know what you're planning,
but stop this.

467
00:35:52,600 --> 00:35:54,360
Leave it to the police

468
00:35:55,440 --> 00:35:57,440
and trust the justice system.

469
00:35:58,360 --> 00:35:59,640
Consider this my warning.

470
00:36:01,960 --> 00:36:03,320
Thanks for the warning.

471
00:36:28,720 --> 00:36:31,600
Gao, was that cop Big Tum?

472
00:36:31,680 --> 00:36:32,640
Yeah.

473
00:36:33,280 --> 00:36:36,200
Is Mungkorn betraying us?

474
00:36:37,080 --> 00:36:40,760
Hong, let's go back to base
and tell everyone he betrayed us.

475
00:36:40,840 --> 00:36:44,960
Wait. We still don't know
why that cop is involved with him.

476
00:36:46,960 --> 00:36:48,200
Stay calm.

477
00:36:48,720 --> 00:36:51,480
Let's wait and hear
what Mungkorn has to say.

478
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:04,160
Here, these are delicious.

479
00:37:04,240 --> 00:37:05,440
Wow, that looks good.

480
00:37:05,520 --> 00:37:07,680
I promise they're really good.

481
00:37:07,760 --> 00:37:09,160
Want some?

482
00:37:09,760 --> 00:37:11,600
Hey, you took it already?

483
00:37:11,680 --> 00:37:13,560
Wait, let's eat together.

484
00:37:13,640 --> 00:37:14,720
They look so good.

485
00:37:14,800 --> 00:37:18,760
Here, there's more.

486
00:37:18,840 --> 00:37:20,520
This one looks good too.

487
00:37:20,600 --> 00:37:21,320
Mom.

488
00:37:22,800 --> 00:37:24,120
Excuse me for a second.

489
00:37:24,640 --> 00:37:28,080
Koh.

490
00:37:28,160 --> 00:37:30,400
Why didn't you tell me you were coming?

491
00:37:31,080 --> 00:37:32,280
I just stopped by for a bit.

492
00:37:32,360 --> 00:37:34,560
I brought you some food too.

493
00:37:34,640 --> 00:37:36,080
Look.

494
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:39,080
You must be busy, huh, Captain?

495
00:37:43,400 --> 00:37:47,240
Working this hard, you'll definitely
make it to the top one day.

496
00:37:49,360 --> 00:37:52,400
I'll go give these snacks
to my friends. Just a moment.

497
00:37:55,720 --> 00:37:59,040
Here, my son brought you some snacks.

498
00:37:59,120 --> 00:38:00,480
-That looks good.
-Croissants.

499
00:38:00,560 --> 00:38:02,480
<i>Do you think your mom would be okay</i>

500
00:38:02,560 --> 00:38:04,280
<i>if she knew what you're doing now?</i>

501
00:38:11,040 --> 00:38:12,920
Have you eaten yet?

502
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:15,640
The aunties want you to join them.
Wanna go?

503
00:38:16,400 --> 00:38:17,880
I already ate, Mom.

504
00:38:18,480 --> 00:38:19,720
Want some coffee? I'll make you some.

505
00:38:20,600 --> 00:38:21,760
Mom.

506
00:38:27,280 --> 00:38:30,840
If I quit being a police officer,

507
00:38:31,880 --> 00:38:32,880
what would you think?

508
00:38:34,840 --> 00:38:38,080
Koh, why would you quit?

509
00:38:40,520 --> 00:38:42,240
You haven't done anything wrong, have you?

510
00:38:45,080 --> 00:38:48,480
I'm just a bit tired, Mom.
I was just asking.

511
00:38:49,080 --> 00:38:53,160
Koh, whatever you choose to do,
change jobs or do anything else,

512
00:38:54,440 --> 00:38:56,160
I won't mind.

513
00:38:56,920 --> 00:39:01,400
As long as you're a good person,

514
00:39:01,480 --> 00:39:03,720
I'll always be proud of you.

515
00:39:06,160 --> 00:39:08,960
I'll go make your coffee. Wait a moment.

516
00:39:28,960 --> 00:39:31,680
SAVINGS ACCOUNT TO E-WALLET

517
00:39:31,760 --> 00:39:33,320
AMOUNT 120 BAHT

518
00:39:33,400 --> 00:39:35,040
CONFIRM

519
00:39:35,800 --> 00:39:36,960
I've paid it.

520
00:39:37,040 --> 00:39:39,120
That's 20 per bag. Here.

521
00:39:39,200 --> 00:39:41,160
Forty. Thanks.

522
00:39:41,240 --> 00:39:42,280
Thank you.

523
00:39:55,520 --> 00:39:57,720
NEXT MISSION: ELIMINATE LOUIS

524
00:40:07,400 --> 00:40:08,520
Yeah, Angpao?

525
00:40:09,200 --> 00:40:10,280
You got the message, right?

526
00:40:10,360 --> 00:40:11,640
Yeah, I got it.

527
00:40:11,720 --> 00:40:13,400
What are you going to do?

528
00:40:25,680 --> 00:40:28,760
I'm glad everyone decided to continue.

529
00:40:30,520 --> 00:40:35,040
When the whole team shows up like this,
doesn't mean you can trust everyone, huh?

530
00:40:41,040 --> 00:40:43,760
Gao, what do you mean? I don't understand.

531
00:40:44,960 --> 00:40:46,880
-I mean…
-Hey.

532
00:40:46,960 --> 00:40:48,080
It's nothing.

533
00:40:48,960 --> 00:40:51,520
Hurry up and tell us
what we're doing this time.

534
00:40:52,040 --> 00:40:53,040
Alright.

535
00:41:03,160 --> 00:41:07,400
<i>Now you all know that Louis</i>
<i>is our target for this mission.</i>

536
00:41:08,440 --> 00:41:10,440
<i>He's running illegal businesses,</i>

537
00:41:10,520 --> 00:41:13,480
<i>gambling dens, call centers,</i>

538
00:41:13,560 --> 00:41:16,320
<i>and recently even opened</i>
<i>a fake pharmacy as a front,</i>

539
00:41:16,400 --> 00:41:19,040
<i>along with an online gambling network.</i>

540
00:41:21,800 --> 00:41:24,000
-That looks familiar, right, Chen?
-Yeah, exactly.

541
00:41:24,520 --> 00:41:26,680
<i>But Louis's real main income,</i>

542
00:41:26,760 --> 00:41:29,840
<i>the one no one knows about,</i>
<i>is money laundering.</i>

543
00:41:30,440 --> 00:41:34,160
<i>Most of his clients are shady businessmen.</i>

544
00:41:34,240 --> 00:41:36,440
<i>When they get illegal money,</i>

545
00:41:36,520 --> 00:41:40,760
<i>they use Louis's network to clean it.</i>

546
00:41:40,840 --> 00:41:43,640
<i>As his money and influence grow,</i>

547
00:41:43,720 --> 00:41:45,520
<i>he's trying to level up,</i>

548
00:41:45,600 --> 00:41:49,920
<i>washing his image</i>
<i>and moving into politics to gain power.</i>

549
00:41:50,440 --> 00:41:52,960
Our first step

550
00:41:53,800 --> 00:41:56,200
is to bring down Louis,
the money launderer.

551
00:41:56,280 --> 00:41:58,640
But don't forget,
his backing is political.

552
00:41:58,720 --> 00:42:02,080
This isn't as easy
as dealing with Boss Kluay or Mam.

553
00:42:02,160 --> 00:42:03,400
That's exactly why we need

554
00:42:03,480 --> 00:42:05,960
to break the trust
between both sides first.

555
00:42:09,400 --> 00:42:12,240
<i>Mr. Wisut Hema-a-thipat.</i>

556
00:42:12,320 --> 00:42:14,560
<i>Owner of VS Group</i>

557
00:42:15,520 --> 00:42:17,760
<i>and a waste recycling business.</i>

558
00:42:18,400 --> 00:42:20,360
<i>But behind the scenes,</i>

559
00:42:20,880 --> 00:42:24,640
<i>he runs one of the biggest</i>
<i>online gambling networks in the country.</i>

560
00:42:26,160 --> 00:42:28,040
<i>Even though he's not a politician,</i>

561
00:42:28,640 --> 00:42:31,560
<i>his financial support to political parties</i>

562
00:42:31,640 --> 00:42:36,440
<i>gives him massive influence</i>
<i>and connections.</i>

563
00:42:37,040 --> 00:42:40,000
Wisut has had
a long-standing relationship with Louis.

564
00:42:40,080 --> 00:42:41,840
And Admin has confirmed

565
00:42:41,920 --> 00:42:43,720
that tomorrow,

566
00:42:43,800 --> 00:42:46,680
Louis will be transporting a large amount
of dirty money from Wisut for laundering.

567
00:42:46,760 --> 00:42:49,400
You want us to steal Wisut's money?

568
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:51,800
We'll make Louis believe

569
00:42:51,880 --> 00:42:53,800
the transfer went through,

570
00:42:54,320 --> 00:42:56,040
even though the money is actually gone.

571
00:42:57,520 --> 00:43:00,920
After the money disappears,
both Wisut and Louis

572
00:43:01,680 --> 00:43:03,440
will think the other side cheated, right?

573
00:43:03,520 --> 00:43:04,720
Exactly.

574
00:43:04,800 --> 00:43:07,960
When the bone
that keeps the dogs fed disappears,

575
00:43:08,480 --> 00:43:11,960
they'll start turning on each other.

576
00:43:25,000 --> 00:43:26,360
Hurry up.

577
00:43:31,600 --> 00:43:32,880
Faster.

578
00:43:34,200 --> 00:43:35,520
Damn it.

579
00:43:35,600 --> 00:43:37,040
Move! I'll handle it.

580
00:43:45,560 --> 00:43:46,600
Here.

581
00:43:47,640 --> 00:43:49,280
Hey, are we done yet?

582
00:43:52,680 --> 00:43:54,520
-Almost done?
-Yes, almost.

583
00:43:54,600 --> 00:43:57,240
-Hurry up. Let's move.
-Yes, boss.

584
00:43:57,320 --> 00:43:58,960
Hey, close up the truck properly.

585
00:44:06,920 --> 00:44:08,240
<i>Louis's method</i>

586
00:44:09,280 --> 00:44:11,800
is to temporarily store the dirty money

587
00:44:11,880 --> 00:44:16,160
at Wisut's waste facility
before laundering it into the system.

588
00:44:16,240 --> 00:44:18,640
<i>That place is heavily secured.</i>

589
00:44:22,000 --> 00:44:24,760
<i>Even though they use garbage trucks</i>
<i>to move the money quietly,</i>

590
00:44:24,840 --> 00:44:26,120
so it doesn't draw attention,

591
00:44:26,200 --> 00:44:30,360
they still have security escorts
driving alongside them.

592
00:44:30,440 --> 00:44:33,080
<i>If anything goes wrong,</i>

593
00:44:33,160 --> 00:44:36,560
or the truck doesn't arrive,
they will immediately report it to Louis.

594
00:44:38,000 --> 00:44:40,280
That's why we must act
without them noticing.

595
00:44:42,080 --> 00:44:44,000
Who's doing what for this mission?

596
00:44:44,600 --> 00:44:47,560
Everyone here has their own role.

597
00:45:17,720 --> 00:45:19,640
<i>The first step</i>

598
00:45:19,720 --> 00:45:21,680
is Angpao and Risa

599
00:45:21,760 --> 00:45:23,600
breaking into the CCTV system

600
00:45:23,680 --> 00:45:25,920
<i>and accessing the factory database</i>

601
00:45:26,000 --> 00:45:28,040
<i>before the money truck arrives.</i>

602
00:45:28,840 --> 00:45:31,720
This isn't easy. The Wi-Fi is blocked.
We can't get through.

603
00:45:31,800 --> 00:45:33,760
What do we do now?

604
00:45:34,480 --> 00:45:37,240
We'll have to reset the network
using a stronger signal,

605
00:45:37,320 --> 00:45:39,680
use the same SSID as the factory router,

606
00:45:39,760 --> 00:45:42,600
and trick their system
with a fake router we set up ourselves.

607
00:45:43,600 --> 00:45:45,600
That's going to take a long time.

608
00:45:45,680 --> 00:45:47,760
About half an hour.

609
00:45:47,840 --> 00:45:51,480
We don't have that much time.
Is there a faster way?

610
00:45:53,400 --> 00:45:55,000
We'll have to go manual.

611
00:45:56,600 --> 00:45:58,000
-Manual?
-Yeah.

612
00:46:07,080 --> 00:46:10,040
The money truck is here. Yak!

613
00:46:10,120 --> 00:46:11,560
Yak, the money truck is here!

614
00:46:12,160 --> 00:46:14,520
Hey, Yak! Are you done?

615
00:46:15,320 --> 00:46:17,800
Hurry up! The truck is here!

616
00:46:21,080 --> 00:46:22,680
Stop messing around! Hurry up!

617
00:46:24,200 --> 00:46:26,560
Move. Stop making those weird sounds.

618
00:46:40,720 --> 00:46:43,600
Wow, there are so many.
How are we supposed to know which one?

619
00:46:44,840 --> 00:46:47,640
There's only one way.
Plug them in one by one.

620
00:46:49,320 --> 00:46:50,920
Which one is it? Is it this one?

621
00:46:58,240 --> 00:46:59,440
No luck.

622
00:47:01,880 --> 00:47:03,280
Is it this one?

623
00:47:03,960 --> 00:47:06,040
This money shipment is large.

624
00:47:06,120 --> 00:47:09,840
Louis will be extra cautious
and send scouts at intervals.

625
00:47:09,920 --> 00:47:14,000
That means our only chance
is inside the tunnel,

626
00:47:14,080 --> 00:47:18,480
to seize the garbage truck
without the escorts noticing.

627
00:47:23,760 --> 00:47:25,520
Okay, ladies and gentlemen.

628
00:47:35,480 --> 00:47:37,280
And once Yak's vehicle is set,

629
00:47:37,360 --> 00:47:41,360
Gao and I will distract the lead escort.

630
00:48:00,960 --> 00:48:02,320
Hi!

631
00:48:03,040 --> 00:48:04,480
Hi, boys!

632
00:48:06,400 --> 00:48:08,080
-What the hell?
-Open the window!

633
00:48:10,440 --> 00:48:12,600
-Hey!
-Hey, calm down.

634
00:48:12,680 --> 00:48:13,960
Let me talk first.

635
00:48:15,080 --> 00:48:16,520
Once you get here,

636
00:48:16,600 --> 00:48:20,360
I'll bring my car in from the side
as close as possible.

637
00:48:22,760 --> 00:48:27,040
So Koh and Chen can jump onto the truck.

638
00:48:29,040 --> 00:48:30,960
This feels like a Jackie Chan movie.

639
00:48:31,040 --> 00:48:34,200
But I'm the one jumping
onto the garbage truck?

640
00:48:34,280 --> 00:48:36,040
-You can do it, man.
-Yeah.

641
00:48:36,120 --> 00:48:37,520
Hey, let's go.

642
00:48:38,160 --> 00:48:39,840
Open the window!

643
00:48:40,560 --> 00:48:42,000
What do you want?

644
00:48:42,680 --> 00:48:45,120
We just arrived in Thailand.

645
00:48:45,200 --> 00:48:48,520
We're wondering where young people
go out these days.

646
00:48:55,160 --> 00:48:57,240
Bonanza moved to Khao Yai.

647
00:48:57,320 --> 00:48:59,720
Center Point is gone.

648
00:48:59,800 --> 00:49:01,640
Hey, no offense.

649
00:49:01,720 --> 00:49:04,480
We were wondering if you

650
00:49:04,560 --> 00:49:07,000
could take us somewhere to hang out.

651
00:49:19,080 --> 00:49:19,960
Here we go.

652
00:49:32,560 --> 00:49:33,600
Koh!

653
00:49:35,040 --> 00:49:36,160
Help me.

654
00:49:47,000 --> 00:49:48,680
Looking for trouble
with overseas kids or what?

655
00:49:48,760 --> 00:49:50,400
What the hell are these people doing?

656
00:49:56,520 --> 00:49:58,080
Something's off.

657
00:50:06,240 --> 00:50:07,680
-Geez!
-Oh my!

658
00:50:07,760 --> 00:50:08,560
Girl.

659
00:50:08,640 --> 00:50:11,240
Don't mind him.
Don't mess with a crazy guy.

660
00:50:11,320 --> 00:50:12,840
It's ridiculous, a total waste of time.

661
00:50:18,760 --> 00:50:19,600
Come on!

662
00:50:23,600 --> 00:50:25,680
You studied abroad
and think you can act tough?

663
00:50:25,760 --> 00:50:27,640
You think you're a big shot?

664
00:50:27,720 --> 00:50:29,360
-Damn it.
-You're really doing this?

665
00:50:29,440 --> 00:50:30,800
-You're done for.
-At your age,

666
00:50:30,880 --> 00:50:32,480
you don't remember your father's name?

667
00:50:32,560 --> 00:50:33,520
You know who my dad is?

668
00:50:34,360 --> 00:50:37,600
Get closer!

669
00:50:38,280 --> 00:50:40,120
Stop the car!

670
00:50:40,200 --> 00:50:41,520
You're in trouble now!

671
00:50:41,600 --> 00:50:43,240
-You crazy idiots.
-Come on!

672
00:50:43,320 --> 00:50:45,320
-Stop the car!
-Go on then, stop the car!

673
00:50:47,000 --> 00:50:48,280
-Go ahead!
-Get closer!

674
00:50:48,360 --> 00:50:49,840
-Come on!
-Get closer!

675
00:50:49,920 --> 00:50:51,320
-You're done for!
-We'll meet outside!

676
00:50:51,400 --> 00:50:53,840
Alright, bro. Stop the act. Split up now.

677
00:50:53,920 --> 00:50:54,840
Got it.

678
00:50:54,920 --> 00:50:56,800
-Okay.
-Circle back and take care of the ones

679
00:50:56,880 --> 00:50:59,080
-who fell off the truck. Handle it.
-Okay.

680
00:50:59,160 --> 00:51:00,560
We'll meet outside.

681
00:51:00,640 --> 00:51:05,040
If anyone got hurt, can you send them
to the hospital or call an ambulance?

682
00:51:05,120 --> 00:51:06,800
I feel bad for them.

683
00:51:06,880 --> 00:51:08,440
Worry about yourself first, Chen.

684
00:51:09,560 --> 00:51:11,440
If Louis realizes it,

685
00:51:11,960 --> 00:51:13,560
everything's over.

686
00:51:27,760 --> 00:51:29,520
<i>After you successfully</i>
<i>take over the truck,</i>

687
00:51:30,120 --> 00:51:33,480
both of you will pose
as the money truck drivers.

688
00:51:35,120 --> 00:51:37,440
You'll drive it
to the waste sorting facility

689
00:51:37,520 --> 00:51:39,440
and make everything look normal.

690
00:51:39,520 --> 00:51:40,600
SOMSAK LAKLAMSAN, SANGA SONGSOMSUAN

691
00:51:42,400 --> 00:51:43,240
No problem.

692
00:51:43,960 --> 00:51:45,560
And what do I do?

693
00:51:46,440 --> 00:51:48,840
You'll monitor Louis's movements.

694
00:51:48,920 --> 00:51:51,960
If Louis suddenly shows up
at the waste facility,

695
00:51:52,560 --> 00:51:54,240
it's game over.

696
00:52:13,280 --> 00:52:14,280
How's everything?

697
00:52:14,360 --> 00:52:17,840
Everything's normal, boss.
We'll arrive in about ten minutes.

698
00:52:17,920 --> 00:52:20,160
Call me again when you get there.

699
00:52:23,720 --> 00:52:27,960
<i>If Louis makes any move,</i>

700
00:52:28,040 --> 00:52:31,120
<i>Mungkorn must report it</i>
<i>to everyone immediately.</i>

701
00:52:34,040 --> 00:52:35,840
Louis is now at the pharmacy.

702
00:52:57,600 --> 00:52:59,360
<i>Where is your gang hiding now?</i>

703
00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:01,320
<i>What gang?</i>

704
00:53:02,680 --> 00:53:04,440
<i>You might be able to fool Louis.</i>

705
00:53:05,520 --> 00:53:06,800
<i>But you can't fool me.</i>

706
00:53:16,720 --> 00:53:20,520
I think they're starting to make a move.

707
00:53:21,480 --> 00:53:22,840
Keep an eye on them

708
00:53:23,360 --> 00:53:25,200
and report back to me regularly.

709
00:53:30,240 --> 00:53:32,640
-Oh no.
-This one still isn't working.

710
00:53:35,200 --> 00:53:38,000
Hey, Ris, relax.
We're professionals. Stay calm.

711
00:53:38,080 --> 00:53:39,360
Alright.

712
00:53:47,440 --> 00:53:50,000
Hello. Risa, can you hear me?

713
00:53:50,080 --> 00:53:51,080
Yes, Chen.

714
00:53:51,160 --> 00:53:52,640
We're almost there now.

715
00:53:52,720 --> 00:53:54,560
-Already?
-What?

716
00:53:57,880 --> 00:53:59,480
Hey, listen.

717
00:53:59,560 --> 00:54:01,960
Just keep your head down so the CCTV

718
00:54:02,040 --> 00:54:03,600
doesn't catch your face, okay?

719
00:54:03,680 --> 00:54:04,720
Wait, Risa.

720
00:54:05,320 --> 00:54:08,560
What do you mean, keep our heads down
so the CCTV can't see us?

721
00:54:08,640 --> 00:54:10,600
That's exactly what I mean. That's it.

722
00:54:10,680 --> 00:54:11,960
Hello? Risa?

723
00:54:12,720 --> 00:54:14,640
-Got it yet? Faster.
-Not yet.

724
00:54:15,160 --> 00:54:17,880
-What's going on, Chen?
-Sounds like

725
00:54:17,960 --> 00:54:20,040
Angpao still hasn't hacked
the CCTV system.

726
00:54:20,120 --> 00:54:22,520
What?

727
00:54:26,360 --> 00:54:27,400
What are you looking for, Chen?

728
00:54:31,000 --> 00:54:33,080
Koh, can we wear this
to disguise ourselves?

729
00:54:33,160 --> 00:54:36,480
Seriously, Chen.
That looks way too suspicious.

730
00:54:36,560 --> 00:54:39,320
Just put on a mask
to cover your face. Hurry.

731
00:54:40,760 --> 00:54:41,880
Here.

732
00:55:04,960 --> 00:55:07,560
What? Why did it go that far in?

733
00:55:15,360 --> 00:55:18,680
Why are you wearing masks? Take them off.

734
00:55:25,200 --> 00:55:27,920
Take off your masks.
Let me see your faces.

735
00:55:34,360 --> 00:55:38,320
-Hey, we got it! Now we're talking!
-Yes!

736
00:55:38,400 --> 00:55:39,840
Hurry, lock in the code!

737
00:55:40,440 --> 00:55:44,760
Sorry, my friend's been sneezing
the whole way. Not sure if it's COVID.

738
00:55:46,160 --> 00:55:48,320
<i>-I see someone's car.</i>
<i>-Whose car? Who's here?</i>

739
00:55:48,400 --> 00:55:51,560
The money truck has arrived, right?
I wanted to see it with my own eyes

740
00:55:51,640 --> 00:55:53,040
<i>that the money has arrived.</i>

741
00:55:53,120 --> 00:55:54,760
How did Louis get here?

742
00:55:54,840 --> 00:55:57,320
Koh, wasn't Mungkorn watching him?

743
00:55:57,400 --> 00:55:59,680
Yeah. Why didn't he report this?

744
00:55:59,760 --> 00:56:02,960
What are you thinking? Just say it.
Everyone almost died because of you.

745
00:56:03,040 --> 00:56:04,760
Are you trying to betray the team?

746
00:56:04,840 --> 00:56:07,400
If anyone still doubts Mungkorn,
then you're doubting me too.

747
00:56:07,480 --> 00:56:11,720
<i>I checked the money myself at the safe.</i>
<i>No one could've taken it.</i>

748
00:56:11,800 --> 00:56:13,320
<i>Unless Wisut is playing tricks.</i>

749
00:56:13,400 --> 00:56:16,080
With evidence like this,
they're bound to turn on each other.

750
00:56:16,160 --> 00:56:18,480
<i>Hey, Louis! Mr. Wisut</i>
<i>sent us to send you off.</i>

751
00:56:18,560 --> 00:56:20,480
<i>We're not the only ones</i>
<i>after Louis anymore.</i>

752
00:56:20,560 --> 00:56:22,440
But we still have to get him.

753
00:57:11,320 --> 00:57:13,440
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
